{"wiki_catalogs":[{"id":"3bcc7439-ccff-4c60-8e2b-b6ee17143479","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","name":"Project Overview","description":"project-overview","prompt":"Create comprehensive content for the Frankie Picasso project overview. Explain the project's purpose as a Node.js full-stack demonstration application combining Express.js backend and React frontend. Document the dual-purpose nature of the project, its educational goals, and the technologies involved. Include the project's architecture philosophy, target audience (beginners learning modern web development), and key learning objectives. Provide context about why this project exists and what developers can learn from it. Use terminology consistent with the codebase and keep content accessible to newcomers while highlighting the technical foundations.","progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"README.md,package.json","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:31:41.6645634+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:32:20.1354+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"6ee0e276-7560-46f1-8cb1-b845e991cd6e","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","name":"Getting Started","description":"getting-started","prompt":"Create comprehensive getting started documentation for the Frankie Picasso project. Include detailed prerequisites (Node.js version requirements), step-by-step installation instructions using npm install, and clear first-run guidance with npm run dev. Document the expected startup sequence, port configuration (localhost:3000), and verification steps to ensure proper setup. Provide troubleshooting guidance for common installation issues, environment setup problems, and development server startup failures. Include screenshots or command-line examples where helpful. Keep the content beginner-friendly while ensuring experienced developers can quickly get up and running.","order":1,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"README.md,package.json","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:31:41.6674062+