Address error handling strategies, response formatting, and server configuration options. Make content accessible to beginners while providing sufficient technical depth for understanding Express.js fundamentals.","order":3,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"src/index.js","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:31:41.6674062+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:33:23.0570703+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"78a5da43-87b2-4a41-917b-0a033c929783","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","name":"Frontend Components","description":"frontend-components","prompt":"Create detailed documentation for the React frontend components. Describe the React application structure starting with main.jsx as the entry point and App.jsx as the primary component. Document the component hierarchy, state management approach, and styling methodology using CSS modules. Explain the Vite integration for development and build processes, including hot module replacement capabilities. Include examples of component composition, prop handling, and styling patterns. Document the development workflow with Vite's fast refresh feature and how changes are reflected in the browser. Address component lifecycle, rendering patterns, and best practices for React development in this project context.","order":4,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"src/main.jsx,src/App.jsx,src/App.module.css","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:31:41.6680312+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:33:00.5581008+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"70d3e734-de5b-4d29-95d1-912be3c6664b","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","name":"API Reference","description":"api-reference","prompt":"Create API documentation for the Frankie Picasso REST endpoints. Document the GET / endpoint which returns a welcome message with application status information, and the GET /api/health endpoint which provides system health check with timestamp. For each endpoint, specify HTTP methods, URL patterns, request requirements, and response schemas. Include example curl commands and browser-based testing approaches. Document the response formats, status codes, and error scenarios. Provide practical examples of consuming these endpoints using different HTTP clients and programming languages. Include rate limiting considerations, security implications, and best practices for API consumption. Address common integration patterns and troubleshooting tips for API connectivity issues.","order":5,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"src/index.js","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:31:41.6680312+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:33:27.7751072+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"5ca4d07c-e291-4e31-a506-5ca7e5f95c1c","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","name":"Development Tools","description":"development-tools","prompt":"Create comprehensive documentation for the development tools and configuration. Document the Vite configuration including development server settings, build optimization, and plugin integration. Explain the Model Context Protocol (MCP) configuration for GitHub AI-assisted development features. Detail the .gitignore configuration and its impact on development workflow. Include environment variable usage, development server hot reloading capabilities, and debugging techniques. Document the relationship between Vite and React development, build process optimization, and production deployment preparation. Address common development workflows, troubleshooting tools, and best practices for maintaining the development environment.","order":6,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"vite.config.js,.mcp.json,.gitignore","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:31:41.6680312+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:33:57.1204675+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"}],"wiki_items":[{"catalog_id":"a779f3d8-a4d5-43f1-8d62-f129f322399f","title":"Application Architecture","description":"application-architecture","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","reference_count":0,"id":"8392adee-4e42-4e1d-b750-b31dbdd9183c","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:32:16.5969193+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:32:16.6045844+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"3bcc7439-ccff-4c60-8e2b-b6ee17143479","title":"Project Overview","description":"project-overview","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","reference_count":0,"id":"11b90cec-324f-46a0-a381-010c113bbc57","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:32:20.1323205+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:32:20.1359671+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"6ee0e276-7560-46f1-8cb1-b845e991cd6e","title":"Getting Started","description":"getting-started","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","reference_count":0,"id":"b09ef0a0-8e46-4326-b237-fc121e396674","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:32:26.8056986+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:32:26.809566+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"78a5da43-87b2-4a41-917b-0a033c929783","title":"Frontend Components","description":"frontend-components","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","reference_count":0,"id":"d15fd505-1b02-45c9-af35-08427a6af83e","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:33:00.5532951+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:33:00.5581008+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"e34aa62d-67c4-439a-bec2-d49096d56cbb","title":"Server Components","description":"server-components","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","reference_count":0,"id":"0bec960b-432a-4683-9218-96a6dfc18b36","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:33:23.0518834+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:33:23.0576058+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"70d3e734-de5b-4d29-95d1-912be3c6664b","title":"API Reference","description":"api-reference","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","reference_count":0,"id":"e81d77d1-c549-4205-a286-fae5481d9887","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:33:27.7711812+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:33:27.7751072+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"5ca4d07c-e291-4e31-a506-5ca7e5f95c1c","title":"Development Tools","description":"development-tools","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904","reference_count":0,"id":"a4d58a30-5a38-4b5a-b1c1-f8790e46eb13","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:33:57.115879+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:33:57.1204675+05:30"}],"wiki_overview":{"content":"Based on my analysis of the Frankie Picasso project, I can now generate a comprehensive overview. This appears to be a minimal Node.js Express application with some Model Context Protocol (MCP) integration.\n\n\u003cblog\u003e\n\n# Frankie Picasso: Minimal Node.js Express Application\n\n## Project Introduction\n\n**Frankie Picasso** is a lightweight Node.js application built with Express.js that serves as a foundation for modern web development. The project demonstrates clean architecture principles with a focus on simplicity and extensibility.\n\n### Purpose Statement\nThe application provides a minimal yet functional backend service that can be easily extended for various use cases, from simple APIs to complex web applications.\n\n### Core Goals and Objectives\n- Demonstrate modern Node.js development practices\n- Provide a clean, modular project structure\n- Showcase Express.js middleware and routing patterns\n- Enable easy integration with additional features\n\n### Target Audience\n- Node.js developers learning modern Express patterns\n- Teams building microservices or RESTful APIs\n- Developers seeking a minimal boilerplate for web applications\n\n## Technical Architecture\n\nThe project follows a layered architecture pattern with clear separation of concerns:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Client Request] --\u003e B[Express Server]\n    B --\u003e C[Middlewares]\n    C --\u003e D[Static Files]\n    C --\u003e E[JSON Parser]\n    C --\u003e F[Route Handlers]\n    F --\u003e G[Response]\n    \n    H[Public Directory] --\u003e D\n    I[HTML Template] --\u003e H\n    J[CSS Styles] --\u003e H\n    \n    K[Environment Config] --\u003e B\n    L[Package Dependencies] --\u003e B\n```\n\n### Component Breakdown\n\n**Core Server Layer**\n- Express.js application instance with ES module support\n- Environment-based port configuration\n- Modular middleware pipeline\n\n**Static Content Layer**\n- Public directory serving static assets\n- HTML template with responsive design\n- CSS styling with dark theme\n\n**API Layer**\n- Health check endpoint\n- Welcome message endpoint\n- JSON response formatting\n\n### Design Patterns\n\nThe application implements several key design patterns:\n\n1. **Middleware Pattern**: Centralized request processing pipeline\n2. **Module Pattern**: ES6 modules for clean imports/exports\n3. **Configuration Pattern**: Environment-based settings management\n\n## Key Implementation\n\n### Main Entry Points\n\n**Primary Application File**\n- Location: `src/index.js`\n- Purpose: Express server initialization and route configuration\n- Features: Environment variable handling, middleware setup, route definitions\n\n**Public Assets**\n- Location: `public/index.html`\n- Purpose: Static HTML content with embedded CSS styling\n- Features: Responsive design, dark theme, centered layout\n\n### Core Modules\n\n**Server Configuration**\n- Express application setup with middleware chain\n- Port configuration with environment variable support\n- Static file serving for public resources\n\n**Routing Architecture**\n- Root endpoint returning welcome message\n- Health check endpoint with timestamp\n- JSON response formatting\n\n### Configuration Approach\n\n**Package Management**\n- `package.json`: Defines dependencies, scripts, and metadata\n- `package-lock.json`: Locks dependency versions for consistency\n- Scripts: Development, production, and testing configurations\n\n**Environment Management**\n- `.gitignore`: Excludes node_modules, logs, and sensitive files\n- `.mcp.json`: Contains Model Context Protocol server configuration with GitHub integration\n\n### External Dependencies\n\n**Core Dependencies**\n- `express@^5.2.1`: Web application framework\n- Development dependencies: Various middleware and utilities\n\n**Dependency Tree Analysis**\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[frankie-picasso] --\u003e B[express]\n    B --\u003e C[accepts]\n    B --\u003e D[body-parser]\n    B --\u003e E[cookie]\n    B --\u003e F[debug]\n    B --\u003e G[depd]\n    B --\u003e H[encodeurl]\n    B --\u003e I[escape-html]\n    B --\u003e J[etag]\n    B --\u003e K[finalhandler]\n    B --\u003e L[fresh]\n    B --\u003e M[http-errors]\n    B --\u003e N[mime-types]\n    B --\u003e O[negotiator]\n    B --\u003e P[on-finished]\n    B --\u003e Q[parseurl]\n    B --\u003e R[path-to-regexp]\n    B --\u003e S[proxy-addr]\n    B --\u003e T[range-parser]\n    B --\u003e U[send]\n    B --\u003e V[serve-static]\n    B --\u003e W[setprototypeof]\n    B --\u003e X[statuses]\n    B --\u003e Y[type-is]\n    B --\u003e Z[utils-merge]\n    B --\u003e AA[vary]\n```\n\n### Integration Points\n\n**Model Context Protocol (MCP)**\n- GitHub integration for AI-powered development assistance\n- Personal access token configuration for secure API access\n- Command execution through npx for server management\n\n**Development Workflow**\n- Hot reloading during development (`--watch` flag)\n- Environment-based configuration management\n- Modular architecture supporting future extensions\n\n### Component Relationship Diagrams\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    A[Express Server] --\u003e B[Middleware Chain]\n    B --\u003e C[Static Files]\n    B --\u003e D[JSON Parser]\n    B --\u003e E[Route Handlers]\n    \n    F[Public Assets] --\u003e C\n    G[Routes] --\u003e E\n    H[Environment] --\u003e A\n    \n    I[GitHub MCP] --\u003e J[AI Assistance]\n    J --\u003e A\n```\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Functionality Overview\n\n**Minimal API Endpoints**\n- Health check endpoint for monitoring\n- Welcome message for basic validation\n- JSON-formatted responses for consistent API behavior\n\n**Static Content Delivery**\n- Responsive HTML template with embedded CSS\n- Dark theme interface suitable for developer tools\n- Centered content layout with system fonts\n\n**Development Experience**\n- Automatic server restart during development\n- Environment variable support for configuration\n- Clean project structure for easy extension\n\n### Implementation Highlights\n\n**Modern JavaScript Features**\n- ES6 modules with import/export syntax\n- Dynamic import.meta.url for path resolution\n- Async/await compatible middleware patterns\n\n**Security Considerations**\n- Proper middleware ordering for security\n- Environment variable usage for sensitive data\n- Git ignore patterns for sensitive files\n\n### Feature Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --\u003e Initialized\n    Initialized --\u003e Running: Server Start\n    Running --\u003e Healthy: Health Check\n    Healthy --\u003e Error: Exception\n    Error --\u003e Running: Recovery\n    Running --\u003e [*]: Server Stop\n```\n\n**Deployment Architecture**\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Source Code] --\u003e B[Build Process]\n    B --\u003e C[Node Modules]\n    C --\u003e D[Production Server]\n    D --\u003e E[Environment Variables]\n    E --\u003e F[Running Application]\n    \n    G[Development Mode] --\u003e H[Hot Reload]\n    H --\u003e D\n```\n\n---\n\n**Sources:**\n- [package.json](package.json)\n- [src/index.js](src/index.js)\n- [public/index.html](public/index.html)\n- [.mcp.json](.mcp.json)\n- [.gitignore](.gitignore)\n- [README.md](README.md)\n\n\u003c/blog\u003e","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:30:24.5240648+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:30:24.5240648+05:30","id":"cc03b847-68bb-40c5-96f6-415c18279324","repo_id":"236b966b-713e-44e8-990b-6fb8cda70904"},"wiki_readme":{"content":"No readme file","gmt_create":"2026-06-24T19:29:42.1460648+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-06-24T19:29:42.1460648+05:30","id":"250e7dec